//   3  SIGNS, MIRROR    a target to the right asks for a right bank, a target above for more back-stick than trim, a slow aircraft gets more throttle; the whole pilot is mirror-symmetric
//   4  THE NEW LAWS, EACH ON MADE-UP NUMBERS   the heading gain is V / (g tau); the climb rate asked for falls with the equivalent airspeed; the bank limit falls with it; the bank compensation and the climb pull are scheduled on (vRef / EAS)^2; the alpha limiter takes the stick off by
//                       kAlpha per radian of (alpha + lead x pitch rate - limit); the equivalent airspeed is V sqrt(sigma); and the trainer's gains name none of them
//   5  STEP RESPONSES   +-300 and +40 m (overshoot under 0.5 m, settled in 25 s, the angle of attack under 7 degrees), at five speed/height pairs; 20, 90 and 170 degrees of turn (no overshoot, bank held to the limit, sideslip under 3.1, altitude held to 10 m), the left turn the right's mirror; speed steps
//                       of +-30 m/s through the engine's spool (no overshoot beyond 0.1 m/s, altitude within 1.5 m)
//   6  A COORDINATED TURN against g tan(bank) / V (to 4%); the climb's cost against W sin(gamma): the throttle feedforward for a 10 m/s climb is the thrust the climb needs, to 20%
//   7  WINGS FIRST, THEN PULL   a 120-degree bank, an inverted start, a nose-high slow start, a 72 m/s start, 30-, 40- and 60-degree dives (the angle of attack under 13.6 degrees in every one), a roll spin and a pitch spin, each flown level; none loses more than the numbers it is held to
//   8  AIR DATA ARE RELATIVE TO THE AIR   a 20 m/s tailwind, a 10 m/s crosswind and a gusty day: the airspeed asked for is held to 7 m/s through the gusts and the altitude to 1 m
//   9  NaN, DETERMINISM, THE FRONT DOOR
//  10  THE TRAINER'S PILOT IS UNCHANGED   three closed-loop flights (one inverted, one diving with spin, all in wind) with the per-tick controls hashed: the number and the three end points are what the committed autopilot produced before the jet existed
